WEBVTT

00:00:00.483 --> 00:00:05.687
Journey nine: request a product. A member sends a shop an order request

00:00:05.687 --> 00:00:10.305
for a product, without payment. This run takes the journey from

00:00:10.305 --> 00:00:12.651
ninety-five percent to complete.

00:00:13.506 --> 00:00:19.320
Joanna is a member. On Luzandre.com she opens the Faith heavyweight tee,

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:24.810
chooses size M and a quantity of two, and presses Request this item.

00:00:25.511 --> 00:00:28.763
The dialog says it first: no payment now.

00:00:28.763 --> 00:00:32.570
Luzandre.com confirms and you pay them directly.

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:38.281
Below are the tee, the size and the quantity, and the shop's ways to get

00:00:38.281 --> 00:00:38.519
it.

00:00:39.221 --> 00:00:44.081
Ship to me needs a shipping address, filled in from the last one she

00:00:44.081 --> 00:00:48.798
used. The estimate reads: item sixty-eight dollars, shipping nine,

00:00:48.798 --> 00:00:52.157
estimated total seventy-seven dollars plus tax.

00:00:52.859 --> 00:00:57.894
She chooses pick up in Leslieville. The address field goes away,

00:00:57.894 --> 00:01:01.907
shipping is free, and the estimate follows at once.

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:06.633
New in this run, the dialog is proved by keyboard alone.

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:11.590
The arrow keys move between the ways to get it, and Escape closes the

00:01:11.590 --> 00:01:13.386
dialog and sends nothing.

00:01:14.088 --> 00:01:17.211
She adds a note and sends the request.

00:01:17.211 --> 00:01:23.047
Request sent to Luzandre.com: Naomi confirms stock and tells her how to

00:01:23.047 --> 00:01:26.334
pay. The keyboard test found a gap here.

00:01:26.334 --> 00:01:31.512
The focus was lost with the form; now it moves to View request.

00:01:32.215 --> 00:01:37.081
Where does it go? The owner finds each order request in Incoming

00:01:37.081 --> 00:01:41.263
requests, under New, and confirms or declines it there.

00:01:42.298 --> 00:01:46.596
Behind the screen, four API tests now prove who is told.

00:01:46.596 --> 00:01:51.891
The owner gets an in-app notification, new order request from Joanna,

00:01:51.891 --> 00:01:57.263
that links to Incoming requests. It reaches the owner's open page as a

00:01:57.263 --> 00:02:02.482
real-time event. The member is told nothing until the owner answers.

00:02:03.336 --> 00:02:07.864
When the shop confirms, the customer is told in the app, and only then

00:02:07.864 --> 00:02:11.874
does the stock go down. And the order appears as a card in the

00:02:11.874 --> 00:02:14.784
conversation between the member and the shop.

00:02:15.642 --> 00:02:20.312
The order request has an eighth acceptance criterion for this, the

00:02:20.312 --> 00:02:24.628
design names the code as built, and journey nine is complete.

00:02:24.628 --> 00:02:29.439
Left for the owner: the visual, responsive and accessibility sweeps.

00:02:29.439 --> 00:02:34.180
Tax is shown as plus tax and never calculated, and Jubilee takes no

00:02:34.180 --> 00:02:34.746
payment.
